Ladybird now hit-tests SVG text by its character cells, as SVG 2 says,
so a point in a cell hits the text whether or not a glyph covers it.

Gecko does the same: SVGTextFrame::GetFrameForPoint() tests the rect of
each TextRenderedRun, in that run’s user space. And so does Blink:
BoxFragmentPainter::HitTestTextItem() tests an SVG text item’s cell quad
(SvgUnscaledQuad()) or its text bounds rect. In Chrome 158.0.8127.36,
Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 (engine-compare), elementFromPoint()
finds the <text> anywhere in its cells, including over blank parts of
Ahem’s “É” and “p” cells.
